WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.610
An eligible administrator asks
for the role, gives a reason,

2
00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:08.550
proves who they are again with a phishing-resistant
sign-in, and waits for approval.

3
00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:13.862
The role then lasts only the window:
four hours at Tier 0, eight at Tier 1.

4
00:00:13.862 --> 00:00:18.538
Eligibility itself expires too,
so it has to be re-authorized.

5
00:00:18.538 --> 00:00:20.451
The platform stops self-approval,

6
00:00:20.451 --> 00:00:24.688
but it won't stop you making the approvers
and the requesters the same group.

7
00:00:24.688 --> 00:00:27.780
So approvers sit outside
the tier they approve,

8
00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:30.238
and Tier 0's sit in the security office.

9
00:00:30.238 --> 00:00:33.038
And approvers have
twenty-four hours, fixed.

10
00:00:33.038 --> 00:00:38.047
The decision for the CISO: staff each
approver group from outside its tier,

11
00:00:38.047 --> 00:00:40.713
at least two people, sized for real hours.

12
00:00:40.713 --> 00:00:43.630
Next, what can quietly undo all this.
